---
import LegalPage from "~/components/LegalPage.astro";
import { localeParams, useTranslations } from "~/i18n";
import { toLanguage } from "~/i18n/config";
import { SITE } from "~/data/site";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return localeParams();
}

const language = toLanguage(Astro.params.lang);
const t = useTranslations(language);
---

<LegalPage
  language={language}
  path="legal/privacy"
  title={t("legal.privacy")}
  metaTitle={t("legal.meta.privacy")}
  description="How TenPrint Software handles personal data on this website and in its macOS applications."
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what {SITE.name} does with personal data on <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong>
    and inside the macOS applications listed on this site. The short version: we collect as little as
    possible, and we never sell or share it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is an independent software studio based in {SITE.country}. For any question about
    this policy or about your data, write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No analytics and no tracking.</strong> There is no Google Analytics, no advertising pixel,
      and no third-party script that profiles you. Fonts are served from our own domain, so no request
      leaves for a font provider.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No cookies for tracking.</strong> The site stores two values in your browser's local storage
      — your chosen theme and your chosen language. They stay on your device and are never transmitted.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host, Cloudflare Pages, keeps short-lived request logs containing
      IP address, user agent, and requested URL. These are used for security and abuse prevention only.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Download counts.</strong> We increment an anonymous counter when a browser or the in-app
      updater requests a <code>.dmg</code> or <code>.zip</code> from this site. We store only the product,
      whether it was a first install or an update, and the UTC day — not IP addresses, cookies, or
      device identifiers. A weekly totals email is sent to our own inbox. We do not profile visitors
      and we do not share these numbers with anyone else.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the support or feedback form, we receive the message you wrote, your email address, and
    the optional name, product, topic, and version fields you filled in. We use them solely to answer
    you and to improve the product you wrote about. The message is delivered to our inbox by email and
    is not stored in any other system, not used for marketing, and never passed to a third party for
    their own purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Support correspondence is deleted once the matter is closed and no longer useful as a record,
    normally within 24 months. You are never added to a mailing list — we do not run one.
  </p>

  <h2>What the applications collect</h2>
  <p>
    Our macOS applications have no accounts and no telemetry. Settings, layouts, and preferences are
    stored in your own user library folder and never leave your Mac. The only network requests an
    application makes are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Update checks</strong> against tenprintsoftware.com, to see whether a newer version
      exists. This sends nothing beyond the standard information contained in any HTTP request.
      If an update is available, the app downloads a signed zip from the same site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Licence validation</strong>, in paid applications only, to confirm that a licence key is
      valid. This sends the licence key and a machine identifier derived on your device.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are processed by an external merchant of record acting as the seller. They collect the
    billing details required to complete the transaction and to meet tax obligations, and they process
    that data as their own controller under their own privacy policy. We receive only the order
    reference, the licence key, and the email address needed to deliver the licence and to provide
    support.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis and your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR we rely on legitimate interest for operating and securing the website, on contract
    performance for delivering purchases and licences, and on legitimate interest for answering the
    messages you send us. You may at any time ask what data we hold about you, ask for a copy, ask us
    to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will act on the request within 30 days.
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your national data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
  If this policy changes in a way that affects you, the updated date at the top of this page will
  change and the change will be described in a note here. On 5 September 2026 we added anonymous
  daily download counters (product, install vs update, UTC day) so we can email ourselves a weekly
  totals report.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
